<title>EGYPT: Amriyah Cement half-yr profit up.</title>
<headline>Amriyah Cement half-yr profit up.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amriyah Cement said on Monday it made net profits of 86.813 million pounds ($25.58 million) in the first six months of the financial year 1996/7, 21 percent up on 71.493 million in the same period of 1995/6.</p>
<p>The years start July 1 and the company has a tax exemption up to the end of this financial year.</p>
<p>The specialist weekly al-Borsa said on Sunday that in the first seven months of the year the company made profits of 103.02 million pounds, against 83.47 million in the same period of the previous year.</p>
<p>Here are the figures released by the company (all in millions of pounds):</p>
<p>				  July-Dec 1996    July-Dec 1995</p>
<p> Sales			    192.334	    179.650</p>
<p> Cost of sales		  107.976	     99.936</p>
<p> Expenses			   9.090	     16.191</p>
<p>Interest and other</p>
<p>   ordinary revenue	    13.276		9.639</p>
<p> Exceptional revenue	    0.562		0.755</p>
<p> Exceptional expenses	   2.293		2.424</p>
<p> NET PROFITS		     86.813	     71.493</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
